    "Initial post-finish audit exposed one false positive for actual Windows absolute python.exe evaluator commands; fixed command classification with regression coverage and retained all exact commands.",
    "Corrected post-finish audit since 2026-09-03T15:00Z: 2 records, 0 warnings; research logger regression suite 4/4 passed and all 322 records validate."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Six mechanically valid 65k runs produced 407,507 physical training hands and 393,216 untouched evaluation hands. Every-update moving reference had mixed slopes and failed final matched plus Standard10-drift gates; static current-KL had positive slopes in all three seeds.",
    "conclusion": "The specific refresh-after-every-PPO intervention is not robust: it was worse than static at final in two of three seeds and seed2 exceeded the preregistered mean-TV drift limit. This rejects refresh interval 1, not NashPG broadly and not learned self-play at larger scale. Static KL(current||initial) remained stable and improved from 16k to 65k in all three seeds, so its scale evidence is promising but not yet externally validated.",
    "decision": "REJECT_SPECIFIC_REFRESH_EVERY_UPDATE; ADMIT_STATIC_CURRENT_KL_262K_SCALE",
    "next_step": "Preregister exact-state, optimizer/replay/pool-preserving continuation of the three static current-KL lineages from their frozen 65k endpoints to roughly 262k cumulative hands. Evaluate the 65k-to-262k geometric slope on untouched multi-anchor both-seat deals and recheck Standard10 drift before any Slumbot gate."
  },
